# Cloudflare Pages Redirects
#
# One rule, and nothing before it.
#
# There used to be a `/static/* /index.html 404` line above this one, written to
# stop the SPA catch-all answering a missing asset with the shell at status 200.
# It carried the assumption that "existing files are served before these rules
# run" — and that assumption was never checked. Cloudflare Pages evaluates a
# wildcard rule at the edge, ahead of resolving the file, so the rule did not
# fire only for assets that were missing: it answered 404 for the shop's own
# JavaScript bundle, every single request.
#
# It took three days to surface because /static/* is served `immutable,
# max-age=31536000`. Every browser that had already loaded a bundle kept using
# its cached copy and never asked again, so the shop looked fine. The moment a
# deploy changed the hash — or a cache was cleared — the browser asked for the
# real file, was told 404, and the store was a blank white page with no
# JavaScript at all. Clearing the cache made it worse, never better, which is
# exactly backwards from how a caching problem behaves and is why it was
# misread as one.
#
# The protection that line was written for already exists where it belongs and
# is tested: the service worker refuses to store any asset whose body is HTML
# (`cacheableAsset` in sw.js), so a shell answered under a stylesheet's URL is
# never cached, however the host chooses to reply.
#
# Nothing may be added above this rule that can match /static/*. The check
# «لا قاعدة تحجب حزمة المتجر عن نفسه» in scripts/verify-layout.mjs enforces it.
/* /index.html 200
